   "Statement": " <b>Occupation</b><br>Pierce County District Court Judge, Position No. 6<br><br><b>Education</b><br>University of Puget Sound School of Law, Juris Doctorate; University of Washington, Bachelor’s Degree in Political Science</p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\"></p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\"><b>Statement</b><br>Judge Williams has had the privilege of serving the citizens of Pierce County for almost 30 years as a District Court Judge and District Court Judge Pro Tem.&nbsp; Judge Williams has earned an exceptional reputation for fairness, integrity and knowledge of the law.&nbsp;</p><p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Judge Williams currently presides over the Civil Department of Pierce County District Court. Many who come to Pierce County District Court are not represented by an attorney.&nbsp; Judge Williams understands the unique challenges unrepresented litigants have and works hard to ensure every litigant receives fair and impartial justice.</p><p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Judge Williams understands the impacts mental health, addiction, and economic disparity have on the court system.&nbsp; &nbsp;Judge Williams has a proven record of public safety, community service and protecting the rights of victims. Judge Williams is honored to serve the citizens of Pierce County. Thank you for your vote.</p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\"></p><p> ",
